<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopold IV, Prince of Lippe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1871–1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopold IV was the last reigning prince of Lippe, ruling from 1905 after the long succession dispute over the principality was settled in favour of his Lippe-Biesterfeld line. He abdicated on 12 November 1918 during the German Revolution, and Lippe became a free state within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a>.</p></div>
